00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:12.660
retention policies as well.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:15.400
So that means you can actually
set it to actually delete

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.362
those snapshots every six hours,
every Monday, or every month.

00:02:18.362 --> 00:02:19.820
MARK MANDEL: Oh,
that's super cool.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:20.710
That's really nice.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.680
Speaking of doing regular things
to compute engines instances--

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.180
there's a new
solution that came out

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.090
called Reliable Task Scheduling
on Compute Engine with Cloud

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:28.670
Scheduler.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.670
So Cloud Scheduler is the
thing we brought out--

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.295
I think it was several
months ago now--

00:02:32.295 --> 00:02:35.290
for doing reliable, basically,
cron scheduling for items.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.387
And there is a
solution here with code

00:02:37.387 --> 00:02:39.970
that talks about how you can use
Cloud Scheduler, sending data

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:41.550
to Pub/Sub on a regular basis--

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.650
[INAUDIBLE] cron, basically--
and then reliably parsing

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:47.273
that or doing something or
some sort of operation on GCE

00:02:47.273 --> 00:02:49.690
with that and making sure that
it works in a reliable way,

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.220
even if some of your
instances go down

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.250
or other things like that.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.470
So if you're looking
to do something

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:55.480
