00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.830
One of the things that's fairly
new-- and I wanted to plug--

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:33.160
that I'm excited
about is Node.js.dev.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:38.560
So Google has very recently
launched the .dev top-level

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:39.400
domain.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.270
And as part of
launching the domain,

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:43.820
which has a number of stages
of access-- so if you really,

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.580
really cared about
getting a domain,

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.980
you could have gotten a couple
of days ago for $11,000--

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:49.190
I think it's now, like, $1,100.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:50.065
JON FOUST: Oh my god.

00:06:50.065 --> 00:06:51.970
MYLES BORINS: And by--

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.030
I think, it's Monday, it
gets down to about $150.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:56.530
So I have a reminder
set for Monday.

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:57.400
[CHIME]

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.230
Hopefully, I can
get a couple I have

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:01.060
on my mind a little cheaper.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.890
Then it goes all the
way down to $15--

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:04.810
will be regular registration.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:08.080
But a number of different
partners as well as

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:12.940
individuals who own IP rights
got early access to domains.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:15.478
And one of those
was Node.js.dev.

00:07:15.478 --> 00:07:17.520
The .dev team reached out
to myself and Franziska

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.890
Hinkelmann, who is another
[? dev-reler ?] who focuses

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.950
on Node.js, asking if we'd
be interested in using it

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.130
for the Foundation.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:28.730
And in six weeks of a sprint,
we put together a static Gatsby

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:29.630
website.

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.420
It is based on a
whole bunch of content

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:33.610
that the project's been
working on for a while.

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:35.830
It's a whole new slew
of getting started

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:38.710
documentation about hey, how
do I get started with Node?

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:40.210
What are some of
the basic concepts?

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:41.710
How do I even do a node?

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:43.690
And so it's a really
great starting place

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.970
for people who want to
learn about Node.js.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:48.160
It's also an open source
project that's available

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.038
on GitHub/nodejs/nodejs.dev.

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:56.440
So if you're looking for a
low-barrier way to get started

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.337
in contributing to
the Node.js project--

00:07:58.337 --> 00:07:59.920
if you like React,
if you like Gatsby,

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.873
if you like playing around with
websites and improving SEO,

00:08:02.873 --> 00:08:04.540
there's lots of
different ways where you

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.813
can come in and get involved.

00:08:06.813 --> 00:08:08.980
JON FOUST: Nice-- what can
we actually expect to see

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.810
on Node.js.dev?--

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:11.625
